n: 3.4
name: form-language
kind: hub
is: Old Form, read and probed with 40 one-line programs at commit b8ff978c9: an S-expression floor of 4 special forms and 287 table rows (221 operations, 66 rewrites) answered by a 34,149-line C seed; 974 .fk and 1,105 .bml files, about 309,000 lines. A 64-bit NodeID whose composite instances are indices in a shared field, not content digests. Two trees for one recipe. fail, stop and timeout all lower to nothing, recovered by attempt. Ice, water and gas have eight uses with no single definition. Proof is an integer pinned in a file header.
limit: Covers the core language, not the 974-file library: the dialect sections form.action, form.route and public, the walker arms, the collector and the JIT emitters were not read line by line. No band was run. Probes ran on one binary on one arm64 macOS machine against a shared field already holding 21.7 million nodes.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.4.1
name: language
kind: hub
is: The executable surface of old Form: four hand-parsed special forms; a table of 221 operations and 66 rewrites; a pure core in ten families pinned by ten laws; first-class functions with capture; units linked by preludes and imports and lowered from a second grammar; a call that answers one record; host doors; two JIT lanes; grammar rules held as data.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.4.1.1
name: special-forms-and-branch-law
kind: observation
is: The old S-expression reader hand-parses four special forms (defn, do, let, if) and the words true and false; no quote, macro or anonymous-function form exists. The if form treats 0 as false and every other integer, every string and every list, empty ones included, as true, and stops the program on nothing.
status: observed
src: 2.1.7#25033,25116,25130,25161,25672-25676
limit: The branch law was probed on one binary (probes empt1 to empt3 and ifnoth). That no other special form exists rests on a search of the reader for its symbol comparisons.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.4.1.4
name: pure-core-and-laws
kind: observation
is: The old interface document commits to a pure core in ten families (numbers, floats, equality, bits, strings, lists, absence and control, kind, records, nodes) and pins ten laws, asked by one band. Strings are bytes over four operations. The core library keeps the recipe of an operation that became native, and bands hold recipe and native equal.
status: observed
src: 2.7.2#19-65 2.7.26#1-12 2.7.5#15-20,90-98
limit: The laws band was not run by the reading; its 34-bit verdict 17179869183 is read from the band's header.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.4.1.6
name: units-and-lowering
kind: observation
is: A unit's closure in old Form is its preludes, declared in a comment line, its imports, and names from a 39-line home index. Each .bml file and each .fk file with a section is lowered by a floor compiler, a 23-unit plain-Form closure, into a .lowfk text memo with dependency fingerprints. 575 of 974 tracked .fk files carry a section [form.bml].
status: observed
src: 2.7.2#10-15 2.7.7#15-19 2.7.34#1-4 2.7.3#202-213 2.7.22#1-60
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.4.1.7
name: cell-call
kind: observation
is: The old body's cell_call(path, argument, deadline_ms) runs a unit inside the calling process and always answers one record: value, out, err, diag, stopped, errors, resident, ms, cpu_us. No exit code and no stderr stream cross: err is empty, a stop crosses as the record stopped {kind, message, recipe, unit}, each diagnostic as a record in diag.
status: observed
src: 2.7.3#17-45,146-158
limit: The document records about 55 ms before a spawned unit starts and 0.1 ms for a resident call of (do 7); these are the old body's own figures, and the reading did not re-measure them.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.4.1.8
name: host-doors
kind: observation
is: The old interface document's target is one table of host doors in ten families (file, path, process, stream, clock, shared, gpu, device, entropy, self): a door answers its value or nothing, the reason is a word read with host_why, a handle is an index and a generation so a stale handle answers nothing, and await is the one place the body blocks.
status: observed
src: 2.7.2#98-135,183-186
limit: The document's order of work does not mark the door table as standing and says per-verb timing is not built yet; the running operation table still holds host operations as primitive rows with aliases.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.4.1.9
name: two-jits
kind: observation
is: The old seed has two JIT lanes: a C lane that compiles pure-float defns and self-tail-call loops at heat 1024, and a page JIT written in the body's language, offered a defn at each multiple of 4096 heat or 32 time samples, which writes AArch64 words and binds them with jit_fn_bind. Each strict operation is one C function both walker and page call.
status: observed
src: 2.1.6#1274-1297,1381-1385
limit: Read from the old body's floor record. The reading did not read the emitters line by line or run the page lane.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.4.1.10
name: grammar-machinery
kind: observation
is: The old body holds grammar as data: a cursor with no tokenizer, patterns (lit, cls, run, seq, alt, opt, cap), templates that build nodes (emit, splice, const), and reversible rules written name ::= pattern => action <= reverse. A Form evaluator on that cursor is a 172-line file, and the form.lift dialect, with infix, is a 112-line rule file.
status: observed
src: 2.7.24#235-271 2.7.23#15-17 2.7.35#9 2.7.31#1-33 2.7.18#22-108
limit: The evaluator's band was not run; its verdict 65535 is quoted from the file header.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.4.2
name: data-model
kind: hub
is: What a value and a node are in old Form: ten value kinds; a 64-bit NodeID of package, level, type and instance in which an integer is its own identity; composites interned by content yet identified by a field index; a recipe held as two different trees; a blueprint with three authorities and a cell with four carriers; 63-bit integers and binary64 floats; an inert wire format; a store that appends and a boot that writes new images.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.4.2.1
name: value-kinds
kind: observation
is: value_kind in the old seed names ten kinds: unknown, null, bool, float, string, closure, record, node_id, list, int. true, false and comparison results have kind int. nothing has kind null and renders as nothing in print and as null in value_str. A record is keyed and mutable in place, and the record table has no collector.
status: observed
src: 2.1.7#19436 2.7.2#95-96 2.7.3#388
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.4.2.2
name: nodeid-word
kind: observation
is: The old NodeID is one 64-bit word: a mode bit, then package 6 bits, level 13, type 12, instance 32. With the mode bit clear the word is the coordinate 1.1.1.i, a 63-bit signed integer held directly, so an integer is its own NodeID. A float32 leaf 1.1.6 holds its IEEE-754 bits as instance; string and float64 leaves hold a kernel-local table index.
status: observed
src: 2.1.11#6-31 2.7.28#28-34 2.7.2#36
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.4.2.3
name: composite-id-is-field-index
kind: observation
is: intern_node(category, children) answers the same word for equal content. The word holds package 0, the category's level and type, and an instance that is a running index in the host's shared node field, not a content digest: a probe read @0.2.99.21759736 while the field held 21,759,736 nodes. Old documents call composite identity local to a kernel.
status: observed
src: 2.7.4#5-6 2.7.11#91
limit: One machine and one shared field; instance numbers are specific to that field.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.4.2.4
name: two-tree-representations
kind: observation
is: A recipe exists twice in the old body: as a content-interned NodeID tree that is observed and never walked, and as a separate tree of 8-bit-tagged C nodes that the reader builds and the walker executes. The old compiler target file says the native JIT should consume the recipe graph directly and that graph execution still uses the walker.
status: observed
src: 2.7.7#47-52 2.1.7#25099-25169 2.7.12#5,9
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.4.2.5
name: blueprint-and-cell-carriers
kind: observation
is: An old-body blueprint has three coexisting authorities: a hand-kept JSON registry the kernel does not read, rows in form-ontology-bp.fk, and the compiled program image. The word cell names four carriers: a persisted named cell identified by domain and name, a tagged list in the core library, an in-process callable unit, and shared-memory cell maps.
status: observed
src: 2.7.8#8-20 2.7.9#11-19 2.7.13#20-28 2.7.5#483-495 2.7.3#17-41 2.1.10#106-110
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.4.2.6
name: numeric-tower
kind: observation
is: Old Form integers are 63-bit and wrap at 2^62; div and mod truncate and stop on zero. Floats are binary64 and mixed arithmetic promotes. make_float32 and make_float64 answer NodeID leaves of kind node_id, a second float form. No bignum, rational, complex or unsigned 64-bit kind exists. (eq 1 1.0) answers 1; (value_eq 1 1.0) answers 0.
status: observed
src: 2.7.2#50-57
limit: Probed on one binary. That comparisons blur beyond 2^53 comes from a private note the reading did not re-verify.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.4.2.7
name: wire-formats
kind: observation
is: FORMBIN2 is the old body's inert node-tree wire format, its codec in the body's language, with ceilings of 64 MiB, 262,144 strings and 1,000,000 nodes and a gate of 13 canonical, 12 malformed vectors. The suffix .fkb also names an unrelated compile cache, fresh by mtime and size when both stand and are over two seconds old, else by a byte digest.
status: observed
src: 2.7.4#3-48 2.7.3#92-93
limit: The conformance gate was not run by the reading; its witness 511 is quoted from the document. The cell document's freshness sentence speaks of a dependency of the image: mtime and size that stand and are older than two seconds mean it is what was parsed, and any doubt reads the bytes and compares the digest.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.4.2.9
name: store-and-boot
kind: observation
is: In the old body a persisted store is a channel of messages in one file: a cell is appended, and lookup keeps the last match for domain plus name. The boot recipe loads an image, registers a channel, and accepts offered cells by writing the seed plus the offers to a new image; writing onto the seed image's own path is refused with 0.
status: observed
src: 2.7.13#59-81 2.7.25#1-3,81-107
limit: Read as source. The boot band was not run; its verdict 9 is quoted from a specification file.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.4.4
name: control-errors-proof
kind: hub
is: How old Form answers, fails and proves. A 66-line core gives the four acknowledgments one discriminator plus hold, census and choice. Underneath, fail, stop and timeout are all the value nothing and attempt is the one recover point. The reason for a stop is dropped by attempt and held as a value only by a cell call. Sentinel values and stale documents remain. Proof is a bit-sum integer pinned in a band's header.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.4.4.1
name: ack-core
kind: observation
is: The old running offer core is 66 lines. The nothing acknowledgment is the value nothing; zero, one and node are interned nodes of blueprints OAC-ZERO, OAC-ONE and OAC-NODE, read by one discriminator, oac-kind. The core adds choice, hold under a patience count, a chain that holds on silence, and a census counting answered apart from silent.
status: observed
src: 2.1.13#5-64 2.7.9#14-19
limit: The band of the core was not run; its verdict 32767 is quoted from the band header.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.4.4.2
name: control-lowers-to-nothing-and-attempt
kind: observation
is: In the lowered offer core of the old body, oac-fail and oac-stop are both (nothing); try and catch become attempt followed by nothing?; choice is recursion over a list of function values. In the choice lane, store and restore are identity functions, a timeout is a spent budget answering nothing, and restoring does not reverse host effects.
status: observed
src: 2.7.22#89-96 2.1.13#26-30 2.7.21#1-2,16-34
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.4.4.3
name: error-three-layers
kind: observation
is: Old Form has three error layers: nothing as an ordinary value; a stop, a named refusal that unwinds to the nearest attempt or ends the program with exit 1; and (attempt x), which answers nothing when x stopped. Under attempt the reason is printed as an organ-health-v1 JSON line, not returned; a cell call holds it as a value, in stopped and diag.
status: observed
src: 2.7.2#52-53,122-125 2.7.3#37-38,51-53,61-63
limit: Probed on one binary. Examples: nth past the end answers nothing; divide by zero and if on nothing stop. The field stopped is a record {kind, message, recipe, unit} and diag a list of records. The cell call is a second recover point: a spent deadline jumps past any attempt the cell holds to the call's own recover point.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.4.4.4
name: surviving-sentinels
kind: observation
is: The old interface document's failure rule for host doors rules out negative codes, an empty string or list for absence, and 0 for refusal. Sentinels still stand elsewhere: str_byte_at answers -1 out of range, ord and the wire writer answer -1, lookup-cell answers a list of zero or one element, and the Form evaluator uses 0 as an empty environment.
status: observed
src: 2.7.2#60,122-126 2.7.5#119 2.7.30#56 2.7.13#75-81 2.7.31#42,50
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.4.4.5
name: docs-versus-behaviour
kind: observation
is: Probes found the old core library's assert cannot fail: it relies on (head (empty)) stopping, and that call answers nothing. Three documented rules are stale: (seq ...) is a listed verb and an unresolved call; let inside a defn body is forbidden on paper and works; eq is documented for integers and nodes and answers 1 on equal strings and lists.
status: observed
src: 2.7.5#527-530 2.7.32#24 2.7.6#93,124-125
limit: Behaviour was probed on one binary built 2026-11-20.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.4.4.6
name: bands
kind: observation
is: A band in the old body is a program that answers a bit-sum integer, each bit one falsifiable claim, held to the verdict pinned in its own header; the sweep also fails a band that exits nonzero. 584 band files are tracked. The axioms file records a broken chain that answered 2097151 with exit 1, the same number as the healed chain.
status: observed
src: 2.7.6#5-7,71-79 2.7.7#8-13 2.1.1#219
limit: No band was run by the reading; a run writes cache files beside sources. Verdicts are quoted from headers and documents.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.4.8
name: keep
kind: hub
is: Six ideas of old Form the reading marks essential for the restart: one absence value with four acknowledgments and one recover point; numbers as coordinates with content interning; recipes and closures as values with natives as measured replacements; three standing boundary contracts and one stated target, the host door; falsifiable claims pinned beside code; grammar rules and the JIT written in the language itself.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.4.8.1
name: one-absence-four-acks
kind: finding
is: Keep nothing as the one first-class absence, the four-valued acknowledgment read by a single discriminator, attempt as the single recover point, and the hold, census and backtrack-with-memory drivers built on them. The old running cores hold all of these in 107 lines over the two facts nothing and attempt.
status: inferred
conf: high
from: 3.4.4.1 3.4.4.2 3.4.4.3 1.1 1.5 1.7.17 1.7.19
limit: Whether fail is the 0 acknowledgment or nothing, and where the reason for a nothing lives, is not settled by the reading.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.4.8.2
name: numbers-as-coordinates
kind: finding
is: Keep the four-field numeric coordinate for issued identities, with a number being its own identity (an integer is 1.1.1.v, a float32 is 1.1.6 with its bits), content interning of composites, and names resolved to coordinates through a codebook so that a name stays a query key.
status: inferred
conf: mid
