n: 3.4.8.4
name: boundary-contracts
kind: finding
is: Keep three boundary contracts standing in old Form and one stated target: a cell call answering one typed record; an inert wire format the language owns, proved by malformed vectors; extension by writing a new image, never rewriting one; and the target, a host door answering a value or nothing, with a reason word and handles carrying a generation.
status: inferred
conf: high
from: 3.4.1.7 3.4.1.8 3.4.2.7 3.4.2.9 1.4 1.7.20
limit: The host door is the target: the interface document's order of work lists the door table without a mark that it stands and says per-verb timing is not built yet, and the reason reader host_why occurs in no tracked file of the old body at b8ff978c9 except that document.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.4.8.5
name: pinned-falsifiable-claims
kind: finding
is: Keep falsifiable claims pinned beside the code they prove, read together with the exit code. Let the bit-sum integer encoding go: a pinned integer shows that an answer is unchanged since pinning, not that the answer is right, and a 34-bit verdict is opaque to a reader.
status: inferred
conf: mid
from: 3.4.4.6 3.4.1.4
