n: 3.4.9
name: drop
kind: hub
is: Six things in old Form the reading marks as history or defect: a second grammar with its lowering memos; a C seed that holds the operation breadth and a full tag space; identity as a local index with several carriers per idea; names resolved against primitives first and directives placed in comments; sentinels, loose truth and a stop reason that attempt drops; state words with no single mechanism.
at: 2026-11-24

n: 3.4.9.1
name: second-grammar-and-memos
kind: finding
is: Drop the second grammar and what exists only because of two: sections inside files, the floor compiler, the .lowfk text memos, and the S-expression as an authoring surface. 575 of 974 files named Form already hold the other grammar in a wrapper, and both lower to the same four special forms. A printable canonical form of a node tree remains useful.
status: inferred
conf: high
from: 3.4.1.6 3.4.1.1 3.4.1.10
